sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch04-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Systems based on numbers that traditional mathematics (e.g. calculus) can analyze completely end up showing only fairly simple behavior; textbook systems are selected for analyzability and therefore are simple.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Number systems fully solvable by analysis show only simple behavior";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 4, “Systems Based on Numbers”; section “The Notion of Numbers” (from p. 115), p. 115. Scope: number-based systems treated in traditional science and mathematics"
}
